re are some customers like seniors or  students that forget their bags either  in their dorm or they our seniors forget  them at home every time customers forget  the reusable bags pile up sitting around  I would say about 10 and we've had a  clear wrap York University Professor  Calvin Lakin researches waste management  and says the ban will have unintended  consequences it's a lot of feel good and  not do good policy a United Nations  study found the Alternatives take more  energy and carbon to make cotton bags  need to be used up to 150 times before  they're considered more environmentally  friendly for reusable plastic bags that  number is 20. paper bags cut down on  litter but in most cases have a larger  impact on the climate the paper  decomposes and releases all of that  methane and or embodied carbon and  Shoppers May wind up buying more Plastic  Products to line their garbage cans or  pick up after pets some search  single-use Plastics are absolutely bad  and some are actually really great but  in order to figure that out we need to  actually do the work we can't just  assume one way or the other questions  about whether banning single-use plastic  is a double-edged sword  tariya isri Global News Ottawa  electric vehicle Ambitions the federal  government's new targets for Ed sales  the Canadian government is accelerating  its targets for electric vehicles by  2026 one-fifth of all Passenger cars  SUVs and trucks sold in Canada will need  to run on electricity and by 2035 every  passenger vehicle sold in Canada will  need to be electric as Ross Lord reports  there's a long road ahead to meet those  requirements  at less than six percent of the light  duty Market in 2021 electric vehicles  are a small but growing piece of  Canada's Auto industry in the last two  years that number has more than doubled  we're happening fastest in Quebec in  British Columbia two provinces that have  regulated sales targets the federal  government is announcing its first major 